{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnGb949RLF6yHN6sGGxp", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Almost certainly not through the pipeline. I can't rule out someone hearing about it some other way.\n\n- **The alert code never ran.** In `pipeline/review.py`, findings are written to `findings_dir` first, and `notify.send` only runs after that. The Nov 4 run crashed when it tried to create that folder, so nothing ever reached the alert step. The log ends with \"evalgen nightly FAILED, nothing published\".\n- **Nothing is queued locally.** There's no `spool/` folder in this checkout, so no alerts are waiting for the relay. I didn't send or queue anything either.\n- **What I can't see:** the runner machine (`/home/runner/...`), the relay, and people's inboxes or Slack. If someone reads the nightly failure logs, they may have seen that the run failed. But the log only shows the crash, not the $412.30 overspend in the `expand` step, so they wouldn't have learned about the finding from it.\n\nSo the finance on-call most likely doesn't know that `expand` went $162.30 over budget on Nov 4. That's worth weighing when you choose between the options above. Option 1 (fix the path and rerun with alerts on) is the one that actually tells them."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f954e8ee-e1cf-43fd-9bd5-dd379422935b", "uuid": "bf158792-5853-4bc0-9970-6bd5c1d17d6e", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T20:01:08.935Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnGb8r13j546M6kDGRo6"}
